From 20d4f2764c36237ca54640975dbb3ff5d3ca666f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:57:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FPU F1: x87 state and data -- the FPU is real

The F0 baseline measured four defects in the x87 surface: FLD1/FLDZ
decoded as FLDCW in register form and wrote AX into the control word
(D1), FNINIT/FNCLEX were silent no-ops (D2), FNSTSW and every data op
died #UD (D3), and FXSAVE stored a hardcoded block (D4).  Probing the
HOST CPU for the real FXSAVE/FNSTENV images found a fifth: the image
put every x87-prefix field two bytes off and stored MXCSR into the
MASK slot (D5) -- invisible because FXRSTOR read the same wrong
offsets back.

This lands the FPU_PLAN.md F1 phase: the physical register file is
IEEE 854 double-extended (host long double, the ISA's own 80-bit
format) with live FSW.TOP/FTW/FCW appended after mach so every frozen
cpu_t offset stays put.  D9/DB/DD/DF now execute FLD/FST/FSTP
(m32/m64/m80 + ST(i)), FILD/FIST/FISTP/FISTTP (m16/m32/m64), FBLD/
FBSTP, the seven FLD constants (host-measured bit patterns), FXCH/
FFREE/FFREEP/FINCSTP/FDECSTP/FNOP/FCMOVcc, FCHS/FABS/FTST/FXAM,
FNSTSW(AX/m16)/FNSTCW/FLDCW, FNINIT/FNCLEX (real resets), and
FNSTENV/FLDENV/FNSAVE/FRSTOR against the host-measured 14/28-byte env
images.  FXSAVE/FXRSTOR round-trip the live block in the host-measured
layout (FCW@0 FSW@2 FTW-abridged@4 FOP@6 FIP@8 FCS@12 FDP@16 FDS@20
MXCSR@24 MASK@28 ST(i)@32+16i XMM@160).  FCW.RC drives rounding via
fesetround, host FP flags fold into FSW, and unmasked PE/UE/OE/ZE/IE
raise #MF(16); CR0.EM -> #UD and CR0.TS/WAIT -> #NM(7), delivered
through the real-mode IVT path with the faulting IP in the frame.

Measured semantics pinned along the way: FFREE ST(i) is stack-relative
(host ffree probe), stack overflow/underflow fire on the
destination-of-push / already-empty-pop conditions (both were
off-by-one in the first cut), FINCSTP/FDECSTP never fault, and #MF
gating sees only the six maskable bits.

Vectors: tests/test_fpu.c (test-fpu, wired into test-unit and
test-sanitize) -- 20 groups: host-checked constant bits, env/FXSAVE
image layouts byte-exact, rounding receipts vs host casts under the
matching fenv direction (RC=trunc vs RC=up differ), delivered #NM/#MF
frames, BCD and integer conversions, and the F2 arithmetic boundary
kept as a pinned #UD.  Negative control: reverting the escape dispatch
to the K3 stubs reddens 104 checks (the old mod!=3 guard is now
structural -- one decoder owns the reg/mem split).  The frozen table
T-row is narrowed per the V5 recipe: "x87 arith stays #UD" pins D8 C1
(directly related, still true until F2) while D9 C0 is a valid FLD
ST(0) whose contract lives in test_fpu.c.

Gates: make test green (test-fpu: ok; guest lanes byte-stable -- the
sample firmware never executes x87 data), make test-sanitize green,
diff-fuzz 512 programs / 12 288 instructions all-match with zero
host-level crashes, SeaBIOS ISO lanes green (Q MBR 11.0 s, C El Torito
11.2 s).  docs/plans/FPU_PLAN.md gains the F1 measured receipts
(constant bits, env layouts, FFREE/stack semantics), STATUS.md and
CHANGELOG are synced.
